                "annotations": [],
                "text": "An analysis of the training examples reveals the following transformation rule:\n\n1. **Left and right border colors:** The leftmost column is filled with one color ($C_{\\text{left}}$), and the rightmost column is filled with another color ($C_{\\text{right}}$).\n2. **Target points:** The interior contains scattered pixels. The target pixels to be transformed are those of the predominant/target foreground color (other colors act as unchanged distractors).\n3. **Distance-based coloring:**\n   - If a target pixel is closer to the left border than to the right border, its color changes to $C_{\\text{left}}$.\n   - If a target pixel is closer to the right border than to the left border, its color changes to $C_{\\text{right}}$.\n   - If a target pixel is exactly equidistant from both borders, it disappears (becomes background `0`).\n   - Any distractor pixels retain their original color.\n\nPlease provide the test input grid!",
